

🔧 CLI Parser Registration Block (Add to cli/main.py)

Insert this inside your evolve sub‑parser definition:

# --- Parallel Evolution Flags ---
evolve_parser.add_argument(
    "--population-size",
    type=int,
    default=16,
    help="Number of individuals in the population."
)

evolve_parser.add_argument(
    "--tournament-size",
    type=int,
    default=4,
    help="Number of contenders sampled per tournament selection."
)

evolve_parser.add_argument(
    "--offspring-per-gen",
    type=int,
    default=16,
    help="Number of offspring generated each generation."
)

evolve_parser.add_argument(
    "--generations",
    type=int,
    default=10,
    help="Number of evolutionary generations to run."
)

evolve_parser.add_argument(
    "--max-workers",
    type=int,
    default=None,
    help="Maximum number of parallel worker processes (default: use all cores)."
)

🧠 How the CLI maps to your parallel engine

These flags map directly into your upgraded function:

evolve_population_parallel(
    initial_design=design,
    limits=limits,
    duration=args.duration,
    dt=args.dt,
    generations=args.generations,
    population_size=args.population_size,
    tournament_size=args.tournament_size,
    offspring_per_gen=args.offspring_per_gen,
    max_workers=args.max_workers,
)

This gives users full control over:

evolutionary pressure (tournament-size)

search breadth (population-size)

search depth (generations)

mutation throughput (offspring-per-gen)

parallelism (max-workers)

Your CLI now exposes the entire evolutionary engine as a tunable, high‑performance optimization system.

